   "priceMinor": 193500,
   "currency": "USD",
   "availability": "sold_out",
   "description": "Product Description Whistle 1928 – Eastern Arabic Edition brings the playful spirit of early black-and-white animation into a more distinctive dial design. This Eastern Arabic edition features Eastern Arabic numerals on the dial, giving the watch a more unusual and collectible character while preserving the vintage charm of the original Whistle 1928 design. Specifications Case Size: 41 mm Lug-to-Lug: 48 mm Strap Width: 22 mm Base Movement: Miyota 9039 automatic movement Module: Patented In-House Jumping-Hour Mechanical Module — Calibre A.FAH-103-2026-JHv2 Display: Animated jumping-hour display with central minutes and running seconds Strap: Leather strap with quick-release system Mechanical Winding Character Whistle 1928 uses the Miyota 9039 automatic movement, which features a unidirectional winding system. To stay faithful to the 1928 steamboat concept, this model uses a custom boat-shaped rotor. Because its weight distribution is different from a standard semi-circular rotor, the automatic winding feel and efficiency may vary depending on the wearer’s wrist movement and daily activity level. Manual winding is recommended before wearing, after periods of non-wear, or during low-activity days. Disclaimer Whistle 1928 is an original creation by LEGER A.FAH, inspired by the public-domain era of early 1928 black-and-white animation. This project is independently designed and produced, and is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to any other company, studio, or brand.",
