   "description": "Product Description Whistle 1928 is a playful mechanical watch inspired by the charm of early black-and-white animation. At the center of the dial, a whistling character comes to life through a custom-developed jumping-hour display. As the hour changes, the animation moves together with the hour indication, creating a small mechanical performance on the wrist. Specifications Case Size: 41 mm Lug-to-Lug: 48 mm Strap Width: 22 mm Base Movement: Miyota 9039 automatic movement Module: Patented In-House Jumping-Hour Mechanical Module — Calibre A.FAH-103-2026-JHv2 Display: Animated jumping-hour display with central minutes and running seconds Strap: Leather strap with quick-release system Mechanical Winding Character Whistle 1928 uses the Miyota 9039 automatic movement, which features a unidirectional winding system. To stay faithful to the 1928 steamboat concept, this model uses a custom boat-shaped rotor. Because its weight distribution is different from a standard semi-circular rotor, the automatic winding feel and efficiency may vary depending on the wearer’s wrist movement and daily activity level. Manual winding is recommended before wearing, after periods of non-wear, or during low-activity days. Disclaimer Whistle 1928 is an original creation by LEGER A.FAH, inspired by the public-domain era of early 1928 black-and-white animation. This project is independently designed and produced, and is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to any other company, studio, or brand.",
